.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_HAMMER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_hammer
.Nd mount a HAMMER file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar special
.Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility attaches the single-volume HAMMER file system on
.Ar special
at mount point
.Ar node .
The kernel must be built with the HAMMERFS option.
HAMMER version 7 volumes mount read-only or read-write.
Multi-volume file systems and volumes that need UNDO recovery are
refused; so is a read-write mount of a volume holding pseudo-file
systems.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl u
Change a mounted file system between read-only and read-write, as
.Fl o Cm update
does.
A change to read-only fails with
.Er EBUSY
while a file is open for writing, unless
.Cm force
is given, which revokes such files.
.It Fl o Ar options
A comma-separated list of options: ro, rw, noexec, exec, nosuid, suid,
nodev, dev, update and force.
Other options are rejected.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr unmount 2 ,
.Xr hammer 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_hammer 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Dx 1.11 .
